{"availability":"available","full":"PinkFrosties/airport-guesser","name":"airport-guesser","description":"Name the airport from a satellite image. Static PWA game.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-04T20:57:10Z","updated":"2026-10-10T22:48:42Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pinkfrosties.github.io/airport-guesser/","topics":["airport","game","leaflet","pwa"],"demo":"https://pinkfrosties.github.io/airport-guesser/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.867Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.867Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.867Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.867Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A static, backend-free guessing game for phone and desktop: you get a satellite image of one airport (zoom in as much as the real imagery allows, never wider than the start view) and five attempts to name it. Every miss shows the distance to the answer, a compass arrow pointing from your guess toward it, and a proximity percentage. There is one shared Daily airport per UTC date, a separate Hard mode, and endless Practice. It is vanilla JS + Leaflet, installable as a PWA, and keeps stats in localStorage."],"features":["Light, Apple-inspired design, responsive on phone and desktop","Zoom fitted per airport to its runway extent, capped at native tile resolution so images stay sharp","Retina-sharp imagery: tiles are requested at the screen's pixel density (up to +1 level), never CSS-upscaled beyond that","Fast loading: only the visible tiles, background preload of the zoom-out view, service-worker tile cache","Desktop layout: image left, guess panel right"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/PinkFrosties/airport-guesser/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2e9dfda8bbc4b6cc67f455b2ce3e9c631f350ef6360cf1d63276256b90fd54ae","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.989Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.989Z","pro